{
 "atom": "net/atoms/std-http-boot-gate.lolo",
 "trait": "BootGate",
 "source": "orbital-rust/crates/orbital-shell-rust/src/host/boot.rs (boot_env_problems and the production refusal) and orbital-server lib.rs boot_env_tests",
 "note": "Twin of the host boot path: production with a problem refuses the boot, elsewhere the problem only warns. The os/getenv effects of INIT and of each READ_<NAME> step are not played (the replay would run them with no grant); READ_USE_MOCK_DATA, the last read, has no effect and is played, and ENV_COLLECTED stands for the ten answers. The replay ignores a case-level entity. The credential-list effect (ENV_COLLECTED with services and no mock) is not played; its answer is stubbed as CRED_LISTED / CRED_UNLISTED, and the services reach the replay in the ENV_COLLECTED payload because the replay ignores case-level config. The Rust twin is boot_env_tests (missing credential and unreadable catalog lines); the line texts come from std-boot-env-check and std-credential-admin, whose own goldens pin them.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "id": "last-variable-collects-all-reads",
   "steps": [
    {
     "event": "READ_USE_MOCK_DATA",
     "payload": {
      "value": "true"
     },
     "expect": {
      "emits": [
       {
        "event": "ENV_COLLECTED",
        "payload": {
         "vars": [
          {
           "name": "USE_MOCK_DATA",
           "value": "true"
          }
         ],
         "services": []
        }
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
